{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-polynomial-observable-subcategory","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:polynomial-observable-subcategory","kind":"definition","title":"Polynomial observable subcategory of a resolution tree","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-skein-turing-machine","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-observable-subcategory"],"tags":["P-vs-NP","resolution-tree","observable-subcategory","markov-trace","complexity","computational-horizon"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.polynomialObservableSubcategory","text":"polynomial-observable-subcategory.md","leanSource":"polynomial-observable-subcategory.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:polynomial-observable-subcategory\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> be a braid on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> strands with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c</code> crossings. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L = \\hat{\\beta}</code> be its closure. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{R}(L)</code> be the Skein resolution tree (<a href=\"#rem:skein-turing-machine\" data-at=\"information-theory/planck-scale-computation\">Skein Turing machine</a>). Fix a polynomial bound <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(c) = c^d</code>.</p>\n<p>The <strong>polynomial observable subcategory</strong> of the resolution tree is the full sub-poset</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{R}^{\\circ}(L, q)\n  = \n  \\bigl\\{\n    x \\in \\mathcal{R}(L)\n     : \n    \\Gamma_{\\mathrm{poly}}\\!(x, A_0) \\neq 0\n  \\bigr\\}.</code></pre>\n<p>The set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{poly}}(x, A_0)</code> consists of degree-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> sections at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x</code> that the Markov trace computes in at most <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(c)</code> Planck steps. This trace restricts to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{R}_{p(c)}</code>. It collects the nodes of the resolution tree from which the degree-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> answer <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P_L(q)</code> is polynomial-time accessible.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/polynomial-observable-subcategory.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.7.4","page":"b/def-polynomial-observable-subcategory","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.PvsNPBoundary.polynomialObservableSubcategory","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/polynomial-observable-subcategory.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
